# Verbatim third-party SPDX boilerplate — legal text we MUST NOT edit. A licence
# derives its force from being byte-identical to the published text, so the
# autofixable rules (typographic apostrophes, terminology) would do real damage
# here; the pair-match rules also false-positive on parentheses inside long legal
# sentences. Path follows the corpus, which moved out of core in the 2.1 cut.
internal/bridge/license/spdx/

# Go templates carry `{{ }}` directives that confuse pair-match rules. The
# generator tests verify the rendered output, which is what humans read.
internal/generators/template/templates/

# Translated feature-fragment sources. The English-tuned rules (terminology,
# common-misspellings) false-positive on natural Spanish and Ukrainian prose
# ("comando" is not a misspelling of "commando"). The assembled
# docs/<lang>/FEATURES.md variants stay linted — they are machine-wrapped in a
# textlint-disable block; these are the human translation sources.
docs/es/features.d/
docs/uk/features.d/
